+When the Agent owner prepares an existing Session for live resume, its JSONL write handle publishes a durable version-2 observation receipt in its writer-owned directory. The live Session exposes the receipt through `observationRecovery` after normal resume preparation. The receipt identifies the writer epoch, the durable recovered prefix, the first position this owner can write, and up to 128 earlier owners. The owner maintains an incremental prefix digest. It syncs a separate witness after a committed batch that can contain a timed question birth. A failed witness publication can be retried after a later committed batch. A successor verifies those intervals against the recovered prefix digest. Salvageable torn records and writes without a verified witness keep unknown birth ownership. Observer reloads leave the writer epoch unchanged. The receipt is separate from the session format. An absent or unverified receipt provides no observation continuity; a receipt failure leaves ordinary session reads and writes available.
